hello my name is david valenta i am the  lvmpd special victims lieutenant in  charge of the animal cruelty unit  in conjunction with the bureau of land  management we are asking for the  public's assistance in an ongoing  investigation into horse shootings at  the cowboy trail rides inside the red  rock conservation area  the first event occurred in january of  2022 and since then there have been  three additional events in march  june in the early morning hours of july  4th these crimes have all occurred at  night  these shootings are intentional and the  suspect is actively concealing his  identity  in the video and photos you will see the  suspect has a ski mask gloves and is  wearing ear protection  the suspect is believed to park in the  area then walk onto the property and go  to the horse corral each horse has been  shot at close range  this suspect should be considered armed  and dangerous  we are asking citizens to watch the  videos and if anything seems familiar  about the suspect or if you have seen a  suspicious vehicle parked in the area or  have any related information please call  the lvmpd's animal cruelty unit at  702-828-3360  or email us at animal cruelty lvmpd.com  if you wish to remain anonymous  call crimestoppers at  thank you for 702-385-5555 time  you
 

